  "id": "COMPOUND:29798 - PROTEIN:6075",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Morolic Acid may interact with the Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2 through multiple indirect pathways. The drug targets the Pigment epithelium-derived factor, which is subsequently targeted by fluticasone and 3-(5-Benzyloxy-3-methylpent-3-enyl)-2,2-dimethyloxirane, both of which ultimately affect the aminopeptidase 2. Additionally, Morolic Acid is also linked to Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which is targeted by neomycin, another compound that influences the same enzyme. These findings indicate that Morolic Acid may modulate the activity of Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2 through a network of downstream targets, possibly by interfering with the cellular processes that regulate this enzyme. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the regulation of protein degradation pathways, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
